---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The notification manager is a toast queue. It shows each toast as a
  <a href='/components/snackbar'><code>wc-snackbar</code></a> in a stack fixed to the viewport at
  <code>placement</code> (<code>top-start</code>, <code>top-center</code>, <code>top-end</code>,
  <code>bottom-start</code>, <code>bottom-center</code> or <code>bottom-end</code>, the default), in the
  browser's top layer, above sticky headers and open modals. A toast is removed from the page once its exit
  animation ends.
</p>

<p>
  Every toast hides itself after its <code>duration</code> (5000 ms by default; the timer pauses while the
  pointer or focus is on it), dismissible or not, unless it has an <code>action</code> or
  <code>duration: 0</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html' cssClasses='demo-container'>
  <wc-notification-manager name='application-manager' placement='bottom-end'></wc-notification-manager>
  <wc-notification-manager name='secondary-manager' placement='top-end'></wc-notification-manager>

  <wc-button id='notification-btn'>Toast</wc-button>
  <wc-button id='notification-btn-dismissible' variant='outlined'>Toast with action, top</wc-button>
  <wc-button id='clear-btn' variant='text'>Clear</wc-button>

  <script is:inline>
    let count = 1;
    let toasts = [];
    document.getElementById('notification-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
      window.dispatchEvent(
        new CustomEvent('peacock-toast', {
          detail: {
            target: 'application-manager',
            title: 'Saved ' + count++,
            intent: 'success',
            subtitle: `This toast hides itself after 5 seconds.`,
            callback: function(id) {
              toasts.push(id);
            },
          },
        }),
      );
    });

    document.getElementById('clear-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {
      window.dispatchEvent(
        new CustomEvent('peacock-toast-dismiss', {
          detail: { notifications: toasts },
        }),
      );
      toasts = [];
    });

    document.getElementById('notification-btn-dismissible').addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelector('wc-notification-manager[name="secondary-manager"]').show({
        title: 'Connection lost ' + count++,
        intent: 'warning',
        dismissible: true,
        subtitle: 'This toast has an action, so it stays until it is closed.',
        action: 'Retry',
      });
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Showing and hiding toasts</h3>

<p>
  Call <code>manager.show(options)</code>, which returns the toast's id, or dispatch a
  <code>peacock-toast</code> event on <code>window</code> from anywhere, with the options in
  <code>detail</code>. The options are <code>title</code>, <code>subtitle</code>, <code>intent</code>
  (<code>info</code>, the default, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>danger</code>),
  <code>action</code>, <code>dismissible</code>, <code>duration</code> and <code>width</code>; the window
  event also takes <code>target</code> (the manager's <code>name</code>; without it the toast goes to the
  manager named <code>global</code>) and <code>callback(id)</code>.
</p>

<p>
  Hide toasts with <code>manager.hide(id)</code>, or a <code>peacock-toast-dismiss</code> window event with
  <code>detail.notifications</code>, an array of ids.
</p>

<h3>Events</h3>

<p>
  <code>close</code> fires when a toast starts to close, with <code>detail.id</code> and
  <code>detail.reason</code> (<code>'timeout'</code>, <code>'action'</code>, <code>'escape'</code> or
  <code>'api'</code>). <code>action</code> fires with <code>detail.id</code> when a toast's action button is
  pressed.
</p>

<h3>Deprecated</h3>

<p>These keep working, log a console warning where noted, and will be removed in 4.0:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>position</code> (warns): use <code>placement</code>. <code>top-right</code> is
    <code>top-end</code>, <code>top-left</code> <code>top-start</code>, <code>bottom-right</code>
    <code>bottom-end</code>, <code>bottom-left</code> <code>bottom-start</code>.</li>
  <li>The <code>notification</code> window event (warns): use <code>peacock-toast</code>.</li>
  <li>The <code>notification-dismiss</code> window event (warns): use <code>peacock-toast-dismiss</code>. The
    old name collided with <code>wc-notification</code>'s own <code>notification-dismiss</code>.</li>
  <li>The toast options <code>variant</code> (warns; use <code>intent</code>, <code>error</code> is
    <code>danger</code>) and <code>timeout</code> (warns; use <code>duration</code>).</li>
  <li>The events <code>notification-manager-action</code> (use <code>action</code>) and
    <code>notification-manager-dismiss</code> (use <code>close</code>).</li>
</ul>

<p>
  Toasts are now in the top layer, fixed to the viewport, so a manager no longer places them inside a
  positioned container; use a separately named manager with its own <code>placement</code> instead.
</p>
